description:
Design a 2-input NOR gate utilizing NAND gates and an inverter. The circuit first generates two intermediate signals by applying NAND operations to each input with itself, effectively creating NOT gates for both inputs. Then, using these intermediate signals, it combines them through another NAND gate, which, due to its configuration, simulates the NOR function, thereby producing the final output that is LOW when either or both inputs are HIGH, and HIGH only when both inputs are LOW.
module top_module(
    input a,
    input b,
    output out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input a,
    input b,
    output out
);wire nand1_out;
wire nand2_out;
wire inv_out;

// Correcting to use NOT gate instead of a custom inverter module
nand nand1(nand1_out, a, a); // Generates NOT a
nand nand2(nand2_out, b, b); // Generates NOT b
not inv(inv_out, nand1_out);  // Using NOT gate for inversion
nand nand3(out, nand2_out, inv_out); // Generate NOR from NAND outputs

endmodule

